<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1)) || (\old(this.get(i)) == null && this.get(i) == null));</code>

This assert statement ensures that for every valid index `i` from the insertion point `index` to the old size of the list, the element at each subsequent index in the updated list is either equal to the element at the previous index in the old list or both are `null`.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(size); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1)));</code>

This assert statement captures the condition that for every valid index `i` from the insertion point `index` to the old size of the list, the element at each subsequent index in the updated list is either `null` and was `null` in the old list, or is equal to the element at the previous index in the old list.
--------------------
